            QUESTION 01
        </div>

        <h3>
            What is the main problem solved by using a database instead of an in-memory collection?
        </h3>

        <div class="choices">

            <div class="choice">
                <span class="letter">A</span>
                <span>It makes C# code shorter</span>
            </div>

            <div class="choice">
                <span class="letter">B</span>
                <span>It prevents the application from restarting</span>
            </div>

            <div class="choice correct">
                <span class="letter">C</span>
                <span>It allows data to persist after the application stops</span>
            </div>

            <div class="choice">
                <span class="letter">D</span>
                <span>It removes the need for MVC</span>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="answer-box">
            <strong>ANSWER</strong>
                <span>C. It allows data to persist after the application stops</span>
        </div>

    </div>


    

